---
import {Image} from 'astro:assets';
import phoneSettings from '../assets/screenshots/settings-phone-r324.png';
import {languages} from '../data/product';
---
<section id="setup" class="chapter"><div class="container setup-layout"><div><h2>Plug in.<br />Make it yours.</h2><p class="section-intro">No soldering. Start with the board, a USB-C data cable and a supported desktop browser.</p><a class="text-link" href="#flash">Go to installer</a></div><ol class="setup-steps"><li><h3>Connect</h3><p>Use a USB-C cable that carries data as well as power.</p></li><li><h3>Install</h3><p>Choose Install firmware, then select the board’s serial port in your browser.</p></li><li><h3>Join</h3><p>Connect your phone to the ScryBar setup network and open its configuration page.</p></li><li><h3>Choose</h3><p>Choose Wi-Fi, a palette and your swipe order. Set the screensaver and backlight timers independently under Display.</p><details class="setup-preview"><summary>See phone settings</summary><Image src={phoneSettings} alt="ScryBar settings on a phone showing the theme preview, brightness sliders and save bar" width={390} height={844} format="webp" loading="lazy" /></details></li></ol></div>
<div class="container language-line"><h3>Time speaks your language</h3><p>Fourteen ways to tell it. Some more dignified than others.</p><details><summary>See all fourteen languages</summary><ul class="language-list">{languages.map(l=><li>{l}</li>)}</ul></details></div></section>
